LOVA Experiment 14 -- the Stage-2 surface, built and measured

==============================================================================
  1. Losslessness -- a projection that loses information is not one
==============================================================================
  round-trips checked:  2150 (60 bench + 10 algorithmic + 5 apps + 1000 generated, x2 for the digram)
  failures:             0
  evaluated after the round-trip: 10/10 identical

==============================================================================
  2. Density on algorithmic tasks (no built-in shortcut on either side)
==============================================================================
  task                        S1    S2  S2+ref    Py
  ----------------------------------------------------
  factorial                   29    25      19    22
  fibonacci                   43    35      27    26
  is-prime                    84    60      43    56
  collatz-steps               70    56      39    51
  sum-to                      32    26      20    24
  power-of-two                33    25      20    25
  gcd-euclid                  28    29      21    22
  count-divisors              68    54      39    31
  multiply-by-adding          36    32      23    28
  divide-by-subtracting       48    37      26    27
  ----------------------------------------------------
  TOTAL                      471   379     277   312

  surface                                    tokens   vs Python
  --------------------------------------------------------------
  Stage 1 (s-expressions)                       471       0.66x
  Stage 1 + best possible table change          409       0.76x   (Exp 13)
  Stage 2 (one char per byte)                   379       0.82x
  Stage 2 + reference digram                    277       1.13x

  **LOVA is denser than Python on algorithmic code for the
    first time.**  Exp 12 measured 0.66x and Exp 13 showed the
    token table could not get past 0.76x; the surface did.

==============================================================================
  3. LOVABench v2 -- the projection Exp 11 made, against the thing
==============================================================================
  measure                                    tokens
  --------------------------------------------------
  Stage 1 (measured)                            866
  Stage 2 estimate (Exp 11 projection)          546
  Stage 2 (measured, one char per byte)         366
  Stage 2 (measured, + reference digram)        322
  Python, pure                                 7370
  Python, sympy                                1732

  ratio                                      vs sympy   vs pure
  --------------------------------------------------------------
  Stage 1                                       2.00x     8.51x
  Stage 2 estimate (Exp 11)                     3.17x    13.50x
  Stage 2 measured                              5.38x    22.89x

  Exp 11 projected 546 tokens where the built surface needs 322:
  it overestimated the token count by 70%, which means it *understated*
  Stage 2's density by that much.  Node count is a poor proxy in
  both directions -- Exp 12 found it erring the other way on
  algorithmic programs.

==============================================================================
  4. Where the remaining tokens go
==============================================================================
  class             tokens   share
  ----------------------------------
  operators            132    48%
  literals              77    28%
  references            63    23%
  separators             5     2%
  ----------------------------------
  TOTAL                277

  Parentheses are gone entirely -- they were 25% of Stage 1.
  What is left is the program: an operator per node and a
  literal per constant.  Further compression means naming more
  frequent subtrees, which fits the surface to the corpus that
  motivated it (Q46), or a fine-tuned vocabulary, which is M8.

==============================================================================
  Experiment 14 -- summary
==============================================================================
  losslessness:   2150/2150 round-trips exact
  algorithmic:    Stage 1 0.66x -> Stage 2 1.13x vs Python (471 -> 277 tokens)
  LOVABench v2:   Stage 2 measured 5.38x vs sympy, 22.89x vs pure Python
                  (Exp 11 projected 3.17x / 13.50x)
